==================================================
CONTEXT
==================================================

Phase 7 established the AgriAcademy foundation.

The current implementation provides video upload functionality, but this is
not sufficient for the instructor experience.

The objective of Phase 7.1 is to transform the existing video/media capability
into a real course authoring foundation.

Do NOT redesign Phase 7 from scratch.

Inspect the current repository and extend the existing implementation.


==================================================
CORE PRINCIPLE
==================================================

A Bunny video is a reusable MEDIA ASSET.

A video is NOT owned exclusively by one course.

The relationship must be:

Video Asset
    ↓
Lesson
    ↓
Chapter
    ↓
Course


The same Video Asset may be referenced by:

Course A → Lesson 1
Course B → Lesson 4
Course C → Lesson 2

Do NOT duplicate the actual Bunny video when reusing it.


==================================================
SUBSCRIPTION / AUTHORIZATION
==================================================

Only users with:

- Pro
- Business
- Enterprise

may create and manage instructor courses.

Users without an eligible subscription must not be allowed to create,
edit, publish, pause, or delete courses.

Do not introduce a default Basic subscription.

The database remains the source of truth for subscription state.

Authorization must be enforced server-side and through the appropriate
Supabase RLS policies.

A user may only manage courses they own or are explicitly authorized to manage.


==================================================
COURSE
==================================================

Implement/complete the course entity and authoring lifecycle.

A course should support at minimum:

- title
- description
- cover/media
- category
- instructor/owner
- publication state
- created_at
- updated_at

Course lifecycle:

DRAFT
PUBLISHED
PAUSED
DELETED/ARCHIVED


Rules:

DRAFT:
Only the instructor/authorized owner can see it.

PUBLISHED:
Publicly discoverable according to Academy rules.

PAUSED:
Temporarily removed from public discovery while retained by the instructor.

DELETED/ARCHIVED:
Removed from active course listings.


IMPORTANT:

Pause and Delete are NOT the same operation.


==================================================
CHAPTERS
==================================================

A course must support multiple chapters.

Example:

Course
 ├── Chapter 1 — Introduction
 ├── Chapter 2 — Soil Preparation
 └── Chapter 3 — Planting


Each chapter must have:

- ID
- course_id
- title
- position/order
- created_at
- updated_at


The instructor must be able to:

- create chapter
- rename chapter
- reorder chapters
- delete chapter


Chapter numbering must be derived from position.

Do NOT use the displayed number as the primary identity.

Example:

position = 1 → Chapter 01
position = 2 → Chapter 02
position = 3 → Chapter 03


If chapters are reordered, numbering updates automatically.


==================================================
LESSONS
==================================================

Each chapter must contain lessons.

Example:

Chapter 01 — Introduction

01.01 — Course Introduction
01.02 — Course Objectives
01.03 — Required Materials


Each lesson should support:

- ID
- chapter_id
- title
- position/order
- video_asset_id
- optional description
- created_at
- updated_at


The instructor must be able to:

- create lesson
- rename lesson
- reorder lesson
- delete lesson
- assign existing video
- upload new video
- replace assigned video


Lesson numbering must be derived from:

chapter.position
+
lesson.position


Example:

Chapter 2 + Lesson 3

→ 02.03


Never hard-code numbering into the data model.


==================================================
REUSABLE BUNNY VIDEO ASSETS
==================================================

Create/use a reusable video asset abstraction.

The database must store the relationship between the Academy lesson and
the Bunny video asset.

The asset should contain the necessary metadata, such as:

- internal asset ID
- Bunny video ID
- playback information
- thumbnail
- duration
- processing status
- metadata required by the existing media architecture


Do NOT store the entire Bunny implementation throughout course components.

Use the existing Phase 4 media architecture.


==================================================
MEDIA LIBRARY
==================================================

Create an instructor-facing reusable Media Library or equivalent capability.

The instructor should be able to:

- view uploaded videos
- see processing status
- see video metadata
- select an existing video
- upload a new video
- reuse a previously uploaded video


Course editor workflow:

Add Lesson
    ↓
Select Video
    ↓
Media Library
    ├── Existing Video
    └── Upload New Video


If an existing Bunny video is selected, create a reference to the asset.

Do NOT upload another copy.


==================================================
BUNNY DELETE RULES
==================================================

This is critical.

Deleting a lesson must NOT automatically delete its Bunny video.

Deleting a chapter must NOT automatically delete its Bunny videos.

Deleting a course must NOT automatically delete Bunny videos that are still
used elsewhere.

Example:

Course A
 └── Lesson 1
      └── Video X

Course B
 └── Lesson 4
      └── Video X


If Course A is deleted:

Video X MUST remain available because Course B still references it.


Only an asset with ZERO remaining references may become eligible for deletion.


Do not blindly hard-delete Bunny media.

Prefer:

Video Asset
    ↓
reference count = 0
    ↓
ORPHANED
    ↓
eligible for cleanup


This creates a safer cleanup model.


